  m_Name: 1800s peranakan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Peranakan Culture and Kebaya 1800s
  info: "The Peranakan (Straits Chinese) community emerged from the intermarriage
    of Chinese immigrants and local Malays, blending traditions into a unique culture.
    They introduced the intricately embroidered kebaya, beaded slippers, and distinctive
    cuisine like ayam buah keluak (chicken with black nuts). Peranakan culture exemplifies
    Singapore\u2019s multicultural heritage and remains a treasured part of the nation\u2019s
    identity."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 88baf38a697df4a01a0ace0cf81a7f9e, type: 3}
